# Prompt Engineering

## Overview

Prompt Engineering is the process of designing, developing, and optimizing prompts to guide Generative AI and Large Language Models toward useful and appropriate outputs for specific tasks.

As part of my AI Practitioner Series, Videos 4–6 focus on Prompt Engineering and how prompting techniques can be applied when developing Generative AI applications.

The three-part series covers the theory behind prompt engineering, practical implementation, prompt templates, structured outputs, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), testing and evaluation, real-world use cases, prompt injection, and security considerations.

The series focuses on understanding how prompts interact with foundation models and how prompt design can be incorporated into a larger AI application rather than treating prompting as simply asking a model a question.

