# Prompt Engineering Best Practices

Several best practices were covered throughout the series.

## Be Specific

Prompts should clearly communicate the task the model is expected to perform.

Avoid unnecessary ambiguity when a specific result is required.

## Provide Relevant Context

Providing relevant context can help the model understand the task and produce a more appropriate response.

## Define the Expected Output

The prompt should specify what the desired output should look like when a particular format is required.

## Use Examples

Examples can help demonstrate the expected input and output patterns.

Few-shot prompting can be especially useful for tasks that require consistent formatting or classification.

## Test Prompts

Prompts should be tested against a variety of inputs.

Testing should include normal cases as well as unexpected, ambiguous, edge, and potentially malicious inputs.

